# then `b: i64` refused, the reverse accepted. An earlier definition read in pass 2 (`_rdef_loser`) leaves the fn's
# records alone: its own return bits, which its body's `return`s are checked against, are `_bx_ldef_bits` (read through
# `_bx_cur_bits`), and its parameter kinds are its slots' only (`_bx_param`). PARSE_FN_DEF saves and restores the pair,
# so it is that definition's alone. CHANGELOG [6.7.16]
